# 31. Documentation Strategy

Documentation should be produced once per meaningful outcome.

During implementation, one living engineering document may be updated.

Do not create a new closeout document for every minor remediation.

A completed outcome requires:

- RCA
- Dependency audit
- Architecture
- Source of Truth
- API contract
- Database/cache findings
- Security evidence
- Capability Inventory where applicable
- Performance evidence
- Browser evidence
- Human-QA evidence
- Regression
- Deployment
- Rollback
- Deferred work

## Documentation-Only Closeout

A documentation-only commit does not require rebuild, restart or redeployment
when no runtime artifact changed.

Reports must distinguish:

- Runtime implementation baseline
- Documentation closeout HEAD
- Served bundle
- Active runtime source

Do not redeploy unchanged code just to make a documentation HEAD appear in a
runtime marker.

Every active Program Slice must maintain one Evidence Ledger inside its living
engineering document.

The ledger must be the current Source of Truth for:

- Base and implementation commits
- Runtime provenance
- Test totals
- Browser evidence
- Human-QA state
- Known base CI debt
- Side-effect counts
- Scheduler/worker fingerprint
- Artemis contract version and integration-readiness state
- Agent role and authority classification
- PR and merge state

Later reports must be generated from the current ledger.

Do not carry forward stale totals or stale commit references from earlier
reports.

