# 32. Parallel Work, Skills and Subagents

Parallel read-only investigation is allowed when it reduces elapsed time.

Good parallel workstreams:

- Backend/security audit
- Frontend/UX audit
- Provider-documentation audit
- Test/regression audit
- Database/query audit

Rules:

- One primary Integrator owns the final architecture
- One Source of Truth remains authoritative
- Subagents must not make overlapping writes
- Subagents must not independently commit to the same branch
- Subagents must not create parallel credential, capability or runtime owners
- All findings must be reconciled before implementation
- Security-critical decisions remain with the Integrator
- Conflicting findings require a stop and resolution

Skills and reusable commands are encouraged for:

- Repository preflight
- Protected-file checks
- Runtime provenance
- Secret scanning
- Browser QA matrix
- Git closeout
- Documentation verification

Reusable automation must simplify the process, not add another approval layer.

