# 35. Verdict Rules

Allowed verdicts:

- REAL WORKING
- NEEDS MORE VERIFICATION
- PARTIAL
- BROKEN
- UNSAFE
- UI ONLY

## REAL WORKING

Allowed only when all required conditions for the declared risk tier and
outcome are satisfied:

- RCA complete
- Dependencies audited
- Source of Truth preserved
- Relevant backend verified
- Relevant database/cache verified
- Security verified
- Runtime verified
- Performance verified where applicable
- Frontend complete
- UX complete
- Tests passed
- Build passed
- Deployment verified
- Browser QA passed
- Human QA passed
- Regression passed
- Git synchronized
- Documentation complete
- No known relevant defect remains

## NEEDS MORE VERIFICATION

Use when implementation appears complete but required evidence or Human QA is
pending.

## PARTIAL

Use when known functionality, UX, testing or integration remains incomplete.

## BROKEN

Use when the primary workflow fails.

## UNSAFE

Use when authorization, secrets, runtime safety or external-side-effect
protection is unreliable.

## UI ONLY

Use when only frontend behavior exists without verified backend/runtime
support.

Do not use REAL WORKING based only on Cursor’s report.

