# 36. Risk-Based Cursor Response Format

The previous 25-section format remains mandatory for:

- Tier 3
- Tier 4
- Shared Foundation work
- Final closeout
- Any task explicitly requesting the full format

Full format:

## 1. Scope
## 2. Out of Scope
## 3. Repository Status
## 4. RCA
## 5. Dependency Findings
## 6. Source of Truth
## 7. Architecture Decision
## 8. Backend Changes
## 9. Database Changes
## 10. Redis/Cache Changes
## 11. Security Changes
## 12. Runtime/Worker Changes
## 13. Frontend Changes
## 14. UI/UX Redesign
## 15. Tests
## 16. Performance
## 17. Browser QA
## 18. Human-QA Handoff
## 19. Regression
## 20. Build/Deployment
## 21. Files Changed
## 22. Commits
## 23. Git Verification
## 24. Remaining Risks
## 25. Final Verdict

For Tier 1 and Tier 2 iterative work, a compact report is allowed:

## 1. Outcome and Scope
## 2. Confirmed Cause
## 3. Changes
## 4. Tests
## 5. Browser QA
## 6. Deployment
## 7. Git
## 8. Remaining Risks
## 9. Human-QA Milestone
## 10. Verdict

For every Agent Program Slice or Agent final closeout, the report must also
include:

- Specialized Agent role
- Artemis authority boundary
- Canonical Agent-to-Artemis contract status
- Contract/schema version
- Market, symbol and timeframe coverage
- Freshness and provenance semantics
- Cross-Agent compatibility findings
- Correlated-evidence family
- Artemis integration-readiness state
- Decision, veto, sizing, feasibility or execution eligibility
- Deferred Artemis work

Do not claim evidence not produced.

Use:

- VERIFIED
- NOT VERIFIED
- BLOCKED
- NOT APPLICABLE

Do not convert assumptions into PASS.

