# 37. Hard Restrictions

- Do not modify Data Hub
- Do not modify protected unrelated work
- Do not reopen closed baselines without explicit approval
- Do not code before the cause and owner are known
- Do not expand beyond the approved outcome
- Do not create duplicate settings
- Do not create duplicate credentials
- Do not create duplicate Connection state
- Do not create duplicate Capability Matrices
- Do not create duplicate runtime state
- Do not create duplicate Agent registries
- Do not create duplicate permission systems
- Do not hardcode frontend authorization
- Do not trust frontend controls for security
- Do not expose Secrets
- Do not log JWTs
- Do not log signed provider requests
- Do not use unauthenticated internal execution routes
- Do not use hidden bypass tokens
- Do not silently force Live into Demo and report success
- Do not enable Live during normal tests
- Do not clear Emergency Stop during normal tests
- Do not perform an irreversible financial operation in automated tests
- Do not call a real provider unless explicitly authorized
- Do not send real notifications unless explicitly authorized
- Do not approve fake or placeholder values
- Do not leave raw i18n keys
- Do not leave undefined/null
- Do not leave dead buttons
- Do not leave endless loading
- Do not leave retry spam
- Do not treat PM2 online as proof of health
- Do not claim Production verification on Staging
- Do not claim Browser QA from code inspection
- Do not claim Human QA from Playwright
- Do not leave completed work uncommitted
- Do not leave completed work unpushed
- Do not leave runtime different from Git without an explicit explanation
- Do not move to the next outcome before the current milestone and closeout
- Do not create pointer or stamp commit chains
- Do not ask the user for repeated approval for low-risk fixes already inside
  the approved outcome
- Do not fragment one useful workflow into unnecessary micro-slices
- Do not let an analytical Agent place or trigger an order directly
- Do not treat all Agent outputs as equal votes
- Do not hardcode equal Agent weights
- Do not count correlated evidence as independent confirmation
- Do not treat stale, unavailable or incompatible evidence as neutral evidence
- Do not allow Artemis to bypass Risk, Portfolio, Liquidity or runtime-safety
  gates
- Do not allow Order Management to decide market direction or profitability
- Do not claim Artemis integration from UI wiring alone
- Do not claim automated-trading readiness before the required maturity stage
  is verified
- Do not enable Live automated trading without explicit Tier-4 authorization

